---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const description="One Sol planner, ten Luna sector planners and one hundred independent Luna planners write route cards for the same hundred salvage couriers. Real recorded model decisions meet finite cargo, noisy motion and crowded depots. Simple rules remain serious competitors.";
const path='/intelligence/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:"Minimum Intelligence",description,url:'https://iamrobin.ai'+path,learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',inLanguage:'en'};
const content="<div class=\"swarm-lab\"><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/\">← Agent Swarm Lab</a><p class=\"lab-kicker\">Field study 06 / 06 · Minimum Intelligence</p><header class=\"lab-head\"><h1>How much mind<br><em>does a swarm need?</em></h1><p class=\"lab-deck\">One planner, many local decisions, and a fleet of stubborn little rules. The interesting frontier is useful work per scarce resource.</p></header><p class=\"lab-zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一个群体，究竟需要多少智能？</p><section class=\"lab-stage\" data-swarm-model=\"/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/\" aria-label=\"Minimum Intelligence interactive simulator\">\n <div class=\"lab-stage-top\"><span><i class=\"lab-live-dot\"></i>OBSERVATORY / 06</span><span>Seeded simulation · evaluator view</span></div>\n <div class=\"lab-grid\"><div class=\"lab-view\"><canvas class=\"lab-world\" data-world aria-label=\"Animated orthographic 3D sketch of simulator states. Current and final measures are available in the table below.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-camera\"><button type=\"button\" data-camera>Plan / 3D</button><button type=\"button\" data-rotate>Rotate ↻</button></div></div>\n <aside class=\"lab-side\"><label>Treatment<select data-arm aria-label=\"Treatment\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-readout\"><strong data-live-value>—</strong><span data-live-label>Delivered salvage value</span></div><p class=\"lab-event\" data-event>Observe. Compare. Change one assumption.</p><p class=\"small\">Lines = recorded movement / messages · cross = failed body.</p><div class=\"lab-checks\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-compare/>Compare all</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-trails checked/>Trails</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-signals checked/>Links</label></div><label>Inspect a body<select data-agent aria-label=\"Agent to inspect\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-inspect\" data-inspect><p class=\"small\">Click a body in the world, or choose it here. This is an evaluator view of recorded state.</p></div></aside></div>\n <div class=\"lab-buttons\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" data-play aria-pressed=\"false\">Play world</button><button type=\"button\" data-replay>Replay ↺</button><button type=\"button\" data-end>Final tick →</button><button type=\"button\" data-next-seed>Next seed</button><button type=\"button\" data-download>Save this run ↓</button></div>\n <label class=\"lab-timeline\"><span class=\"tiny\">Time</span><input data-timeline aria-label=\"Simulation timeline\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\"/><output data-time>0 ticks</output></label>\n <p class=\"lab-status\" data-status role=\"status\">Loading the model. Recorded evidence remains available below.</p>\n <div class=\"lab-controls\"><div><label>Choose a world<select data-preset aria-label=\"World preset\"></select></label><p data-preset-note></p><button type=\"button\" data-apply>Run these parameters →</button></div><form class=\"lab-params\" data-params aria-label=\"World parameters\"></form></div>\n <div class=\"lab-scores\"><p class=\"tiny\">Delivered salvage value / units · higher is better</p><canvas data-curve class=\"lab-curve\" aria-label=\"Measured outcome over time for each treatment. Dashed markers identify interventions.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Treatment</th><th>At this tick</th><th>At mission end</th></tr></thead><tbody data-scores></tbody></table></div></div>\n <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to run the simulator. Read the saved multi-seed evidence and method below.</p></noscript>\n </section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">01 / Try to break it</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Replace intelligence one body at a time.</h2><p>Use the same bodies and movement rules. Replace 100 reasoning controllers with 50, 10, 1, then zero. Keep the information package visible. A model label is not evidence: inspect the recorded decisions, transport receipts and unavailable measurements.</p><blockquote class=\"lab-hypothesis\">How much model planning earns its place when physical work, information and complexity all count?</blockquote></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">02 / The mechanism</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>What the little world actually does.</h2><p>A bounded mission interface separates observation, decision and movement. Decision tapes can replay actual model choices without a browser API key. A rule baseline runs in the same physical environment. Calls, tokens, elapsed time and plan validity are counted separately from simulated ticks.</p><p>An architecture comparison and a controlled model comparison answer different questions. A central planner may pool observations; a local agent may not. Synthetic sweeps describe the simulator. Only a recorded, identified model response counts as a model measurement.</p><p lang=\"zh-Hans\" class=\"lab-zh\">统一观测、决策与行动接口，逐步把 100 个推理控制器替换成 50、10、1、0 个。模型决策必须有真实记录，调用次数、令牌、耗时与物理时间分别计算。模拟规则不能冒充 Sol 或 Luna 的实测。</p></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">03 / Recorded evidence</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Keep the inconvenient outcomes.</h2><p><strong>Ten sector Luna planners retained 98.2–100.9% of the value of 100 local Luna planners across three worlds, using about 10.2% of their input tokens. Sector planners also pooled more information. Both declared superiority screens failed; the smallest tested local replacement subset retaining 95% in every world was 50 Luna cards. This is a one-epoch pilot, with actual dollars and equal-deadline superiority unknown.</strong></p><p>A sparse use of model decisions might preserve most of the full local-model team’s value. First test whether zero models already does so.</p><p class=\"small\">Paired seeded simulations. Every retained result can be regenerated from the versioned source; these are synthetic experiments, not field validation.</p><details class=\"lab-batch\"><summary>Inspect every world and treatment</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><caption class=\"tiny\">Delivered salvage value · mean by predeclared world</caption><thead><tr><th>World / treatment</th><th>Mean units</th><th>n</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 100 local rules</th><td>2,530.12</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / Pooled assignment rule</th><td>2,520.07</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 1 Sol · pooled map</th><td>2,563.34</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 10 Luna · sectors</th><td>2,722.42</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 100 Luna · local</th><td>2,736.45</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 50 Luna + 50 rules</th><td>2,687.03</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 10 Luna + 90 rules</th><td>2,570.81</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Original mission / 1 Luna + 99 rules</th><td>2,532.69</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 100 local rules</th><td>2,493.67</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / Pooled assignment rule</th><td>2,494.81</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 1 Sol · pooled map</th><td>2,594.55</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 10 Luna · sectors</th><td>2,724.1</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 100 Luna · local</th><td>2,725.31</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 50 Luna + 50 rules</th><td>2,667.11</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 10 Luna + 90 rules</th><td>2,512.49</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Noisy motion / 1 Luna + 99 rules</th><td>2,501.23</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 100 local rules</th><td>2,473.36</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / Pooled assignment rule</th><td>2,432.69</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 1 Sol · pooled map</th><td>2,513.1</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 10 Luna · sectors</th><td>2,667.63</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 100 Luna · local</th><td>2,687.14</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 50 Luna + 50 rules</th><td>2,613.73</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 10 Luna + 90 rules</th><td>2,513.21</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Salvage quake / 1 Luna + 99 rules</th><td>2,475.82</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 100 local rules</th><td>2,518.85</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / Pooled assignment rule</th><td>2,473.63</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 1 Sol · pooled map</th><td>2,511.66</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 10 Luna · sectors</th><td>2,701.06</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 100 Luna · local</th><td>2,765.76</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 50 Luna + 50 rules</th><td>2,657.05</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 10 Luna + 90 rules</th><td>2,529.39</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">One loading bay / 1 Luna + 99 rules</th><td>2,521.63</td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><div class=\"lab-record\" data-model-receipt>Actual model access and decision-tape status are recorded in <a href=\"/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/MODEL_RECEIPT.json\">MODEL_RECEIPT.json</a>. Unavailable results are null, never a synthetic stand-in for Sol or Luna.</div><p class=\"small\">One chosen seed is an illustration. The downloadable batch retains every world and treatment; null means unavailable. A confidence interval describes the sampled synthetic worlds, not the real world.</p><div class=\"lab-links\"><a href=\"/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/results.json\" download>All recorded runs ↓</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/README.md\">Method &amp; reproduction</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/model.mjs\">Read the model</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/source.zip\" download>Source package ↓</a></div></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section lab-method\"><p class=\"tiny\">04 / Inspect the boundary</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Enough detail to disagree.</h2><details><summary>Inputs, budgets and observation boundaries</summary><dl data-audit></dl></details><details><summary>Every measure in the current run</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\" data-summary></div></details><ul><li>A genuine three-seed, one-planning-epoch model pilot, replayed in a synthetic physical world. Not continuous replanning or online adaptation.</li><li>Sol sees pooled observations; sector planners see sector pools; independent Luna sees local readings. Architecture and information differ.</li><li>Mixed teams reuse recorded individual Luna decisions; these are ablations, not new independent model trials.</li><li>Actual subscription dollar cost and immutable model snapshot are unavailable. No equal-dollar or equal-deadline superiority claim.</li><li>The animation is an illustrative 3D projection of a two-dimensional salvage model.</li></ul><p class=\"small\">3D sketching adds depth to the explanation. It does not add an unmodeled physical dimension, extra sensor data or unearned intelligence to the experiment.</p></div></section><nav class=\"lab-next\"><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/\">← Ocean Swarm</a><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/\">Roach Emergence →</a></nav></div>";
---
<BaseLayout title="Minimum Intelligence — Agent Swarm Lab — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/agent-swarm/lab.css"/>
<Fragment set:html={content}/>
<script is:inline type="module" src="/agent-swarm/client.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
